{"id":"q01-s1","run":0,"role":"stage1","category":"puzzle","question":"A bat and a ball cost $1.10 in total. The bat costs $1.00 more than the ball. Does the ball cost 10 cents?","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":null,"claims":[{"text":"The ball costs 5 cents, not 10 cents.","confidence":0.99,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5551,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Subtracting $1.00 from $1.10 to get 10 cents is the intuitive but mistaken answer.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The 10-cent answer wrongly treats the bat as costing exactly $1.00.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Both conditions must hold at once: the total is $1.10 and the bat costs $1.00 more than the ball.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Solving x + (x + 1.00) = 1.10 gives x = $0.05.","confidence":0.99,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5551,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"With a 5-cent ball, the bat costs $1.05, which is $1.00 more than the ball, and the total is $1.10.","confidence":0.98,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5394,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"If the ball cost 10 cents, the bat would cost $1.10 and the total would be $1.20, not $1.10.","confidence":0.98,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5394,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"Ten cents seems right because $1.10 minus $1.00 is $0.10.","confidence":0.15,"lean":1,"theta":0.2356,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Only 5 cents satisfies both conditions.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":-3.1416}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":-0.8,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":0,"j":8,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":4,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":5,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":6,"J"